# DAY 23 — Agent Routing Examples

| # | User Request | Tool Selected | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | What are your business hours? | search_faq() | User is asking a common FAQ |
| 2 | Do you provide home delivery? | search_faq() | User is asking about a business service |
| 3 | Show me all interested leads | get_leads_by_status() | User wants leads with a specific status |
| 4 | Find my new leads | get_leads_by_status() | User wants leads filtered by status |
| 5 | Give me all contacted leads | get_leads_by_status() | User wants leads with a specific status |
| 6 | Write a follow-up for Rahul | draft_followup() | User wants a follow-up message |
| 7 | Create a message for Priya who is interested in AI automation | draft_followup() | User wants a personalized follow-up |
| 8 | Draft a follow-up for Amit, whose status is interested | draft_followup() | User wants a follow-up based on lead information |
| 9 | What payment methods do you accept? | search_faq() | User is asking a common business question |
| 10 | Show me leads that are qualified | get_leads_by_status() | User wants leads filtered by status |

## Routing Rule

The agent should identify the user's goal first.

- General business question → search_faq()
- Request for leads by status → get_leads_by_status()
- Request to create a follow-up → draft_followup()

## Important

The agent should not randomly select a tool.

It should choose a tool based on the user's request and the tool's defined purpose.